#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128972 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "798800a5-255a-5738-91d2-21c2a78e4fb5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Function Is Positive or Negative Using a Sign Table"}] :question/id #uuid "51d10b95-2ba8-5125-8f0d-b21455269c1e" :question/math-academy-id "e-9419" :question/problem "Consider the expression $f(x,y) = -3xy^2$. What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)$?\n\n| $y > 0$ |  |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $y < 0$ |  |  |\n|  | $x< 0$ | $x> 0$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0$. These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2076/Source/Images/fa0cdfbb8ecb9b5d13af631848b5da0c.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2076/Source/Images/f6e83f9a06ec3ffc2e748ac277b18d98.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-3x$ | $y^2$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2076/Source/Images/924be9539b8d5080971b034ecf97ac9f.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y > 0$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $y < 0$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n|  | $x< 0$ | $x> 0$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "490982ac-6197-58eb-8d94-2ef28d659d50" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Function Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/id #uuid "0dea7752-3eb9-58d5-bdd9-50ec96e8d9b6" :question/math-academy-id "e-9423" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y) = -6x^2y$. Determine the region that gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y) \\geq 0$?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0$. These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2076/Source/Images/bd25ddaae705f22bf898f72975a3bad8.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2076/Source/Images/be2358a1616b4922da71ba80f0abb9b3.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-6x^2$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to\n\n$$\nf(x,y) \\geq 0\n$$\n\nusing the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2076/Source/Images/b56ef32af055eb1c45a9ebeeee43aa12.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "798800a5-255a-5738-91d2-21c2a78e4fb5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Function Is Positive or Negative Using a Sign Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9540b1c6-1f60-5074-bc72-614497b1d511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $−$ |\n| $+$ | $−$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125937} {:answer/id #uuid "225ef1cc-e171-581b-9168-b62af522eaaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $+$ |\n| $−$ | $−$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125938} {:answer/id #uuid "474e66ca-38c6-57e5-867b-dc2131699afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| $−$ | $−$ |\n| $+$ | $+$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125939} {:answer/id #uuid "4da82025-9d7b-5d93-8eaa-aa9a7a748046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| $−$ | $+$ |\n| $+$ | $−$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125940} {:answer/id #uuid "7e15f2e9-414c-53a7-b3cf-a14270732414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $−$ |\n| $−$ | $+$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "225ef1cc-e171-581b-9168-b62af522eaaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $+$ |\n| $−$ | $−$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125938} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c61e26d-991b-5668-80f7-0785c37f283e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125936}] :question/id #uuid "044d4f72-bfa3-5995-a255-529e2a3f6304" :question/math-academy-id "q-121237" :question/problem "Consider the expression $f(x, y) = 2x^{2}y$. What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x, y)$?\n\n| $y > 0$ |  |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $y < 0$ |  |  |\n|  | $x < 0$ | $x > 0$ |"}]}
